WEBVTT

00:23:28.413 --> 00:23:30.204
the Great Recession of 2009.

00:23:31.121 --> 00:23:32.621
That was when the world fell apart.

00:23:32.996 --> 00:23:34.288
You could feel it everywhere,

00:23:34.288 --> 00:23:37.913
you could feel it walking around New York
and when all those folks started

00:23:37.913 --> 00:23:39.496
graduating the class of 2009,

00:23:40.038 --> 00:23:43.163
there were so many articles about
how they were just doomed.

00:23:43.246 --> 00:23:47.663
This was a generation that I completely
had the rug pulled out from under them.

00:23:48.288 --> 00:23:51.413
The research that was available
about recessions was ominous.

00:23:51.871 --> 00:23:54.913
A setback at the start of a
career cast a long shadow.

00:23:55.496 --> 00:23:59.704
People who graduated in recessions
continued to earn less. A decade later,

00:23:59.954 --> 00:24:05.413
it's not only that you suffer now, but
that you will also continue to suffer,